#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Hyprchroma's Icons framework: Reversal or Yaru for every Omarchy theme.

Every Omarchy theme points at one icon theme, Omarchroma-Icons, in ~/.icons. Its
Inherits= line names the color variant of the chosen base set (Reversal or
Yaru) nearest the active theme's accent, -dark on a dark theme, so a theme
change rewrites one line rather than renaming anything. Folder icons are
recolored from the active theme: its sidebar highlight, its accent, or its
window border. App icons the base set does not ship can be covered with
Reversal's rounded plate.

Yaru ships its folders as PNG only, so they are traced to SVG once (the
vectorize section below) and then recolor by hex like Reversal's do.

Started by bin/hyprchroma, which holds the sync lock around apply and revert.
Every file written goes through the safe-io block shared with the other
helpers: a verified parent directory descriptor, an exclusive temporary, and a
rename relative to that descriptor, so nothing swapped into a path redirects a
write.
"""

